WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.337
Let’s walk through Communications.

00:00:02.337 --> 00:00:06.475
Use communications for deliberate coordination with a known audience.

00:00:06.475 --> 00:00:09.537
Verify the recipient and purpose before sending, and keep

00:00:09.537 --> 00:00:12.838
rulings or requests that require durable workflow history in their

00:00:12.838 --> 00:00:15.400
owning artifact or RFI surface.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.100
On this slide, send injects, announcements, and

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.375
guidance to all teams, one team, or a

00:00:20.375 --> 00:00:21.812
specific role.

00:00:21.812 --> 00:00:25.062
In practice, verify the recipient before sending;

00:00:25.062 --> 00:00:28.550
broad visibility is an operator choice, not a default

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:28.712
.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:32.335
When you are ready, use Open Communications to move

00:00:32.335 --> 00:00:33.822
to the live surface.

00:00:33.822 --> 00:00:36.560
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:36.710
.
